      "narrative": "SV Kanaalstad are a selling club and good at it. Profit on player sales of €28.2m was more than half the club's €51.2m revenue, led by D. Achterberg's €15.3m move to Serie A and C. Brennan's €8.1m sale to Ligue 1. Revenue covered total costs of €47.9m for an operating profit of €3.3m, and the sales lifted the net profit to €24.9m. Over three seasons the club has taken €38.6m more from transfers than it has spent.\n\nThe profits have gone straight onto the balance sheet. Net assets have risen from €35.1m in 2020 to €121.5m, debt is €6.3m, and €14.2m of cash on its own covers current liabilities. Wages are a controlled 54% of revenue and the distress score is zero.\n\nSecond place on the second-largest wage bill is what that spending should buy, and Europa League qualification looks likely. A campaign would lift revenue by around a quarter on our sample projection. Squad costs, at 69% of revenue, are just inside UEFA's 70% limit, so one or two expensive signings would tip the club over it.",
