      "narrative": "FC Polderburg are third on less than half the revenue of a typical club in the division, a strong return on €17.3m of income. Revenue covered total costs of €17.1m with €0.2m to spare, and €2.3m of profit on player sales lifted the net profit to €1.9m. The club has made a net profit in each of the last five years.\n\nThe balance sheet has grown steadily. Net assets have more than doubled from €5.5m in 2020 to €12.6m, debt is down to €1.0m, and current assets cover current liabilities about one and a half times. Cash of €1.6m is thin in absolute terms, but the distress score of 10 is low.\n\nConference League football is possible. On our sample projection it would add around 12% to revenue, but squad costs already stand at 70.5% of revenue, marginally above UEFA's 70% limit, which the club would need to address. Wages have edged up from 60% to 62% of revenue since 2020, so there is little room for extra signings.",
